      "message": "I\u0027m not sure to understand what this does.\n\nlocks can either be FLASH_CR_LOCK or FLASH_CR_OPTLOCK.\n\nIf locks \u003d FLASH_CR_LOCK:\nSTM32_FLASH_CR ^ FLASH_CR_OPTLOCK \u0026 (FLASH_CR_LOCK | FLASH_CR_OPTLOCK)\n\nSo that\u0027ll return error if FLASH_CR_LOCK is set (makes sense: unlock failed), or if FLASH_CR_OPTLOCK is unset (why?)\n\nIf locks \u003d FLASH_CR_OPTLOCK:\nSTM32_FLASH_CR ^ FLASH_CR_OPTLOCK \u0026 FLASH_CR_OPTLOCK\n(that seems to be equivalent to !(STM32_FLASH_CR \u0026 FLASH_CR_OPTLOCK))\n\nSo that\u0027ll return error if FLASH_CR_OPTLOCK is unset (again, why?)",
